cicada play [score.cicada] [--audio tymbal|oto|null] [--max-resident-pcm <size>]

play and watch a score

Flags:
  --audio <name>             select tymbal, oto, or null
  --max-resident-pcm <size>  cap on decoded sampler-pack PCM held in memory, such as 512MiB (default 1GiB)
  --help                     show this help

CICADA_AUDIO selects the backend when --audio is omitted. Tymbal is the default on Windows and Linux; oto is the macOS default. Use --audio oto to select oto explicitly. Sampler packs stay in memory as decoded float32 PCM, and --max-resident-pcm caps their total; a score whose packs decode to more is refused, with the cap and the size measured in the message. A reloaded score holds its own copy of the packs until it takes over at the next bar. Sizes are whole numbers with KiB, MiB, GiB, KB, MB or GB, such as 512MiB.
